</ul><h1>Never Outta Outlets</h1><p>Just the other day, we sold a product that was three charging pads in one. A single plug, three spaces for charging your stuff. And then there are all the power banks we’ve had on here that essentially provide a charge <em>anywhere</em> to multiple devices.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, with just one device, such as a Roku or a Fire TV Stick, you can have access to more television and movies than you’d ever be able to watch. Or maybe your television comes with this technology built-in. And even if you wanted to run your sound through external speakers, there’s a chance these are chargeable and bluetooth, meaning they don’t need to be plugged into anything.</p>
<p>What we’re getting at is that your outlets <em>should</em> be less crowded than ever these days.</p>
<p>Which means: you should need fewer of these things now than ever before.</p>
<p>And yet, there’s always something.</p>
<p>You get a game system and an inclination to start watching the local news every morning, resulting in your purchase of a digital antenna, and now things are starting to get a bit cramped behind your TV. Or you buy a printer for your home office, and all of a sudden, it’s constant outlet triage between your laptop, your bluetooth speaker, and your aforementioned three-spot charging pad.</p>
<p>There could also just be a layout issue. Even in a newly built home that’s apparently optimized for convenient living, you occasionally find that the only good place for your favorite recliner and reading lamp is in <em>this</em> corner, and the only place for the TV is along <em>that</em> wall, and there’s just one outlet between them.</p>
<p>And then, don’t get us started on power surges! Those pesky things!</p>
<p><em>Deep sigh</em></p>
<p>Okay, can we level with you all? We’re running out of steam here. Everything we said is true and provides a compelling-ish reason to purchase these. But, like, C’mon. Who cares?</p>
<p>It’s a two-pack of surge protectors. They’re totally good, totally simple. Bunch of outlets on each one, plus a couple USB-A ports, and a USB-C. In other words, there’s just not much to it.</p>
<p>If you need some surge protectors, get them. If you don’t, don’t.</p>